(Regression: reaped, waiting, process, and child must remain usable as
 ordinary identifiers - this repo shipped exactly this regression once
 before, when `send` was claimed unconditionally and broke user functions
 of that name. `the reaped status` is consumed only as that exact phrase;
 `the reaped` followed by anything else is an ordinary variable
 reference. `without` is already a distinct token, so `print ... without
 newline` is unaffected. `waiting` is an ordinary identifier everywhere
 it is not the reap suffix.)

a number called waiting is 7.
a number called reaped is 99.
a number called child is 5.
a number called process is 11.
Print "waiting {waiting}".
Print "reaped as variable {reaped}".
Print "the reaped as variable {the reaped}".
Print "child {child}".
Print "process {process}".
Print "no newline here" without newline.
Print " continued".